# Cost plan of a small building

A treemap draws each item as a rectangle whose area is its cost, nested inside its group. The
sheet adds up the groups and works out the share of the structure. Costs are in thousands.

```mermaid
treemap
"Building"
    "Structure"
        "Foundations": 120
        "Frame": 310
        "Floors": 260
    "Envelope"
        "Facade": 280
        "Roof": 90
    "Services"
        "Mechanical": 220
        "Electrical": 150
        "Hydraulic": 80
```

## Groups
C_structure: 120 + 310 + 260 | structure
C_envelope: 280 + 90 | envelope
C_services: 220 + 150 + 80 | services
C_total: C_structure + C_envelope + C_services | total

## Shares
s_structure: C_structure / C_total -> % | structure
s_envelope: C_envelope / C_total -> % | envelope
s_services: C_services / C_total -> % | services
